From 929ea7a4e6b15e50541cf429091b821d1282745e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 13:55:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(db): warm connections and one round trip less per
 custom-timeout query (958)

Every step of a chat turn is a multiple of ~145 ms, one round trip to the
database. Three things cost small-talk turns round trips they did not need:

- pg closes an idle connection after 10 s by default, so a turn after a
  short pause opened connections afresh (TCP, TLS, auth: ~6 round trips).
  The database counted 10-25 new sessions a minute. Idle connections are
  now kept 5 minutes with TCP keepalive; max_connections is 2091.
- A query with its own timeout waited for the SET that restores the
  default after its rows had arrived. The restore now runs before the
  connection goes back to the pool, but the caller no longer waits.
- Small talk read the conversation for "discuss first" before learning it
  is small talk; the answer is "no goal" either way, so it is checked first.

The pools also get an error listener: a dropped idle connection used to be
an unhandled 'error' event, which ends the process.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HwFREQwL5g9E6qRrUf9bau
